   "source": [
    "# Classes and Objects 1\n",
    "\n",
    "A class in Pythona template defined by\n",
    "the user so that they can create objects and other instances of the objects\n",
    "\n",
    "It simplifies complex programming by grouping data togehter and organizing it"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9d9eb973-fa17-4559-baa4-6039f7a554fe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- defining a class"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "3ec0b7f0-d0a6-44e8-b559-cdd86c3fcb56",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class Dogs:\n",
    "    sound = 'bark' # an attribute of the class"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "680dbece-2136-4e6f-a1c7-952a6d30ccc7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- creating an object form the Dog class"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "968c4593-dcb0-47ed-91f3-aea0b5d8bab5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "bark\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dogs = Dogs()\n",
    "print(dogs.sound) \n",
    "# accessing the class attribute , its like youve created\n",
    "# a new syntax"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "9a02ce32-ab09-4c85-8494-f37b74663f1a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Buddy\n",
      "3\n",
      "German Shepard\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# __init__ function \n",
    "class Dog:\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, name, age, species): # initialises name,age, speices\n",
    "        self.name = name  # Instance attribute of the Dog class\n",
    "        self.age = age # Instance attribute of the Dog class\n",
    "        self.species = species # Instance attribute of the Dog class\n",
    "\n",
    "# Creating an object of the Dog class\n",
    "dog1 = Dog(\"Buddy\",3,\"German Shepard\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(dog1.name)  # Output: Buddy\n",
    "print(dog1.age) # Output: 3\n",
    "print(dog1.species)  # Output: Canine"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fc4630b5-67c6-42df-aaa1-2c03a205df58",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### self parameter and __ str __\n",
    "\n",
    "- the self parameter allows us to access the ttributes and methods of the\n",
    "object\n",
    "\n",
    "- When print(dog1) is called, Python automatically uses the __ str __ method to get a string representation of the object. Without __ str __ , calling print(dog1) would produce something like <__main__.Dog object at 0x00000123>."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "64bf6291-f533-4ffb-9a3c-5bc95a999e63",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Buddy is barking!\n",
      "Buddy is 3 years old\n",
      "John is 7 years old\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "class Dog:\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, name, age, species): # initialises name and age\n",
    "        self.name = name  # Instance attribute of the Dog class\n",
    "        self.age = age # Instance attribute of the Dog class\n",
    "        self.species = species # Instance attribute of the Dog class\n",
    "    def bark(self): \n",
    "        print(f\"{self.name} is barking!\")\n",
    "    def __str__(self):\n",
    "        return f\"{self.name} is {self.age} years old\"\n",
    "# with this , whenever we type dog1.bark it produces a string that says\n",
    "# Buddy is barking!\n",
    "# Creating an instance of Dog\n",
    "dog1 = Dog(\"Buddy\", 3,\"Canine\")\n",
    "dog2 = Dog(\"John\", 7,\"Corgi\")\n",
    "dog1.bark()\n",
    "print(dog1)\n",
    "print(dog2)"
   ]
  },
